### ============================================================================
### IaC Deployment Assistant — HITL Workflow on Azure Durable Functions
### ============================================================================
### Pipeline: input_router → drafter → reviewer (HITL pause) → publisher
###
### The reviewer executor validates the Terraform, summarizes it, and pauses
### for human approval. On rejection, the drafter re-generates incorporating
### feedback. On approval, the publisher pushes to ADO and creates a PR.
###
### Prerequisites:
### 1. Start Azurite: azurite --silent --location .
### 2. Start Durable Task Scheduler emulator
### 3. Configure local.settings.json (copy from local.settings.json.template)
### 4. az login
### 5. Run: func start
### ============================================================================


### 1. Start a new IaC workflow.

POST http://localhost:7071/api/workflow/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "service": "App Service",
  "region": "westeurope",
  "options": "Linux plan, Standard S1 tier, with Application Insights",
  "recipient_email": "aminelemsih@microsoft.com"
}

### Another example — Storage Account with CDN.

POST http://localhost:7071/api/workflow/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "service": "Storage Account",
  "region": "francecentral",
  "options": "Blob containers for media and backups, plus a CDN endpoint",
  "recipient_email": "aminelemsih@microsoft.com"
}

### ============================================================================
### 2. Check Workflow Status
### ============================================================================

@instanceId = 1c4e03016dfc49438fa965896a96b632

GET http://localhost:7071/api/workflow/status/{{instanceId}}

### ============================================================================
### 3. Approve the Terraform Review
### ============================================================================

@requestId = 152ede0d-0f60-4bbd-b705-639edb0f62bc

POST http://localhost:7071/api/workflow/respond/{{instanceId}}/{{requestId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approved": true,
  "feedback": "Looks good, deploy it."
}

### ============================================================================
### 4. Reject and Request Changes
### ============================================================================
### The reviewer will re-draft incorporating your feedback.

POST http://localhost:7071/api/workflow/respond/{{instanceId}}/{{requestId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approved": false,
  "feedback": "Use Premium v3 plan instead of Standard S1, and add a custom domain."
}

### ============================================================================
### Health Check
### ============================================================================

GET http://localhost:7071/api/health

### ============================================================================
### 5. Chat with the Orchestrator Agent
### ============================================================================
### The orchestrator collects the 4 required fields (service, region, options,
### recipient_email) then triggers the workflow via HTTP tools.

POST http://localhost:7071/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "I want to deploy a Linux App Service with Application Insights in westeurope. Send the summary to aminelemsih@microsoft.com."
}

### Continue the conversation (reuse thread_id returned by the previous call).

@threadId = 43b15b8d-6be9-4663-b84e-635b2c3d6e89

POST http://localhost:7071/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "thread_id": "{{threadId}}",
  "message": "yes"
}

### Ask for the status of a running deployment.

POST http://localhost:7071/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "thread_id": "{{threadId}}",
  "message": "what is the status?"
}

### Approve the review through the chat (the orchestrator calls respond_to_review).

POST http://localhost:7071/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "thread_id": "{{threadId}}",
  "message": "approve, looks good"
}

### Reject through the chat with explicit feedback.

POST http://localhost:7071/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "thread_id": "{{threadId}}",
  "message": "reject: use Premium v3 plan instead of Standard S1"
}